<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date> dcterms:title "planned end date" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDate"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Used for anything with a planned end date, such as when a lease will expire, when an offer is no longer available, etc. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date that something is or was planned to end, with precision of one day." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n204 ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date_time> dcterms:title "planned end date time" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDateTime"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "This is an abstraction over the various precisions of planned end time, and is not expected to be asserted directly. Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes." , "This property, unlike gist:actualEndDateTime, does not have a subproperty for microsecond precision, because planned times typically are not expressed at that level of granularity. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date_time"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date that something is or was planned to end, with no implied precision." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/end_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDateTime"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_minute> dcterms:title "planned end minute" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndMinute"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Used for things like meetings and time card entries, where the hour and minute are important. Recommended usage is to zero out the seconds and microseconds to avoid spurious precision.Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_minute"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date and time that something is or was planned to end, with precision of one minute." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n335 ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndMinute"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_year> dcterms:title "planned end year" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndYear"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Used for anything with a planned end date where precision of one year is sufficient. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Note that it is not valid to zero out months and days, so arbitrary values must be included." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_year"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date that something is or was planned to end, with precision of one year." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n52 , _:c14n69 ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndYear"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date> dcterms:title "planned start date" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDate"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Used for anything with a planned start date, such as when a lease will start, when a configuration becomes available, etc. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date that something is or was planned to start, with precision of one day." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n86 ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date_time> dcterms:title "planned start date time" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDateTime"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "This is an abstraction over the various precisions of planned start time, and is not expected to be asserted directly. Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes." , "This property, unlike gist:actualStartDateTime, does not have a subproperty for microsecond precision, because planned times typically are not expressed at that level of granularity. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date_time"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date and time that something is or was planned to start, with no implied precision." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/start_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDateTime"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_minute> dcterms:title "planned start minute" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartMinute"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Used for things like meetings and time card entries, where the hour and minute are important. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the seconds and microseconds to avoid spurious precision." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_minute"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date and time that something is or was planned to start, with precision of one minute." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n79 ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartMinute"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_year> dcterms:title "planned start year" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartYear"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Used for anything with a planned start date where precision of one year is sufficient. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Note that it is not valid to zero out months and days, so arbitrary values must be included." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_year"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The date that something is or was planned to start, with precision of one year." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n276 , _:c14n61 ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date_time> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/datetime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartYear"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes> dcterms:title "precedes" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedes"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "The less-than symbol is often used to represent this relation." , "This is the transitive version of gist:precedesDirectly." , "Typically this predicate would be used asymmetrically and irreflexively, but the ontology does not formalize this." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "A generic ordering relation indicating that the subject comes before the object." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Any> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedes"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:transitive true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes_directly> dcterms:title "precedes directly" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedesDirectly"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "If two items in an ordered collection share the same position, they both directly precede the following element." , "It is safest to use this property only when the directness has a semantic correspondence with the world. Only break a direct link by inserting an intermediate item when that change corresponds to a change in the world." , "Typically this predicate would be used asymmetrically and irreflexively, but the ontology does not formalize this." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes_directly"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "A generic ordering relation indicating that the subject comes immediately before the object." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes> ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Any> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedesDirectly"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/prevents> dcterms:title "prevents" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:editorialNote "See guidance on removing this term in the next major release at https://github.com/semanticarts/gist/issues/1380#issuecomment-3617257248" ;
	skos:exactMatch "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prohibits"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prevents"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n247 ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/prevents"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:deprecated "gist marks this term owl:deprecated." ;
	linkml:deprecated_element_has_exact_replacement "prohibits"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Relates an intention to behavior that it prohibits." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Intention> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Intention> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n63 ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Intention> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Behavior> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prevents"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/prohibits> dcterms:title "prohibits" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prohibits"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "A behavior can be prohibited without being prevented. For example, a speed limit may prohibit driving faster than a stated speed but does not always succeed in preventing drivers from exceeding that speed." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/prohibits"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Relates an intention to a behavior that it forbids or seeks to prevent." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Intention> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Intention> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n252 , _:c14n293 ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Intention> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Behavior> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prohibits"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/provides_order_for> dcterms:title "provides order for" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/providesOrderFor"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/provides_order_for"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Links a member of an ordered collection to the real-world item it represents in that collection." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/OrderedMember> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/OrderedMember> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/OrderedMember> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Any> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/providesOrderFor"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/range_includes> dcterms:title "range includes" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:broadMatch "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/rangeIncludes"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "There may be multiple rangeIncludes assertions on a single property." , "This property is used to guide the ontology user; like all annotation properties, it does not play a role in inference." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/range_includes"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Relates a property to a class that is an expected type of its values." ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n136 ;
	linkml:implements "owl:AnnotationProperty"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/string> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/rangeIncludes"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/refers_to> dcterms:title "refers to" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/refersTo"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/refers_to"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Relates something to another resource that it points to, indicates, or references." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Any> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/refersTo"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/requires> dcterms:title "requires" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/gist_core> ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/requires"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "This predicate is defined generally enough to encompass a few different meanings of the English word 'requires':\n\n  1. To need something or to make something necessary.\n  2. To order or demand something, or to order someone to do something, especially because of a rule or law.\n  3. To make it officially necessary for someone to do something.\n\nImplementations requiring a more specific meaning should define subproperties." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/requires"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The subject needs the object or makes it necessary, mandatory, or compulsory." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:examples _:c14n296 ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GistThing> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Any> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/requires"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/sequence> dcterms:title "sequence" ;
